0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`click.edit(filename=...)` now accepts a single `os.PathLike[str]` or any iterable of `str` and `os.PathLike[str]`. `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_termui.py` passes (259 passed, 23 skipped). I read the diff, which matches the spec.\n\n- **`src/click/termui.py`:**\n  - Added `import os`.\n  - Widened the `filename` annotations.\n  - The body now wraps a `str` or `os.PathLike` in a one-item tuple.\n  - Added the docstring sentence and the 8.5.0 `versionchanged` entry.\n- **`src/click/_termui_impl.py`:** only the `edit_files` annotation changed. Its body needed no change, because `subprocess.Popen` takes path objects in the argument list.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** added the entry at the end of the `Unreleased` list.\n\n- **One overload, not two:** the spec says to change both `@t.overload` signatures, but only one of them has a `filename` parameter. The other is the text-mode overload, so the implementer changed the one that exists plus the implementation.\n- **Typing test not checked:** I did not run `tests/typing/typing_edit.py` through a type checker. Neither `mypy` nor `pyright` is installed in `.venv`, and the spec's required command doesn't include it.\n- **Line length:** the two new `filename` annotation lines in `termui.py` are longer than 88 characters. I didn't run a formatter or linter on them.", "ttft_ms": 1977, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 6950, "uuid": "1bc6aa3d-86f0-4ccd-83c6-301c4d74ec92", "ttft_stream_ms": 1685, "time_to_request_ms": 15, "first_content_frame_ms": 1685, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
